⟦ docs_lifecycle_proposal | PROPOSAL-v1 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-10-04T17:33:18Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status active

// docs/ LIFECYCLE — study + taxonomy (rmw3 2026-10-04: "estudiar el ciclo
// de vida de la documentacion que migramos... pasar a runtime lo que se
// pueda"). Evidence-based census of the 1255 files in docs/ after the
// migration circles (papers, drift, migration).

@problem

docs/ currently mixes five natures under one roof:
  records, narrative, LIVE LOGIC (specs bound by instance.vsm),
  frozen duplicates of system/, and runtime artifacts.
Result: the transient layer cannot be trusted as "just documentation",
and logic that should be evaluated by system/kernel sits inert in text.

@census_2026_10_04

  276  frozen-in-place (spec_revision 249 + archive + canon_mirror)
  258  artifacts (pdf/png/json/html/tex/bib — evidence companions)
  235  records (sessions, findings, experiments, evaluation, correspondence)
  170  narrative markdown
  122  technical docs (deploy, infra, operations, vsf-bbh, corpus...)
   74  other/uncategorized
   55  ACTIVE plans/governance (incl. system_backlog, second_order_repair — bound by instance)
   47  LOGIC CANDIDATES (spec/internal/governance/deploy carrying predicate|spec(|rule(|ante:)
   18  runtime python (experiment analysis scripts)
  VSM versions: 372 at 1.2.1 vs ~430 legacy (1.0/0.3/0.1/...) + 9 undeclared
  system/: 120/120 already at 1.2.1 (fully normalized)
  overlaps: 71 basenames shared docs/<->system/ (samples byte-identical:
    covenant.vsm 282=282, definitions_core 139=139, agent_policy 56=56)
  instance.vsm binds DIRECTLY into docs/ (plan/, spec/, theory/, internal/,
    governance/ anchors) — some docs are live instance components
  kernel today: 3 InvariantCheck + covenant checks (thin runtime surface)

@lifecycle_model

  state diagram (VSM-recursive, validation at EVERY transition):

  INBOX(born, proposed)
    --normalize to vsm-1.2.1 + classify-->  CLASSIFIED
    CLASSIFIED --> ACTIVE (system/: spec in a level dir with
        classification.local + bindings from instance + predicates
        EVALUATED by gates/backbone)
    ACTIVE --> KERNELIZED (its predicates exist in vos_kernel runtime:
        covenant / invariants / regulation / backbone predicates —
        the document's logic is now ENFORCED, not merely declared)
    KERNELIZED --> CONSIDERED (verified: logic present in system AND
        runtime-enforced in kernel — doc no longer carries unique truth)
    CONSIDERED --> ARCHIVED (docs/archive/<cycle>-<ts>/ with reason line;
        removed from active census, kept as provenance)
    INBOX --> RECORD (sessions/findings/experiments/evidence: born and
        dies in docs/, never promotes — IS the epistemic record)
    INBOX --> NARRATIVE (papers/theory/outreach/guides: docs/ is their
        legitimate home — no promotion path)
    INBOX --> RUNTIME (.py runnable, state json/jsonl: moves to its
        runtime home per doctrine — packages/, scripts/, state/)
  LEGACY VALIDATION rule: any file touched by a transition must end at
  @vsm 1.2.1 (write-gates enforce on commit; untouched legacy files are
  debt, not silent).

@decision_tree_R10

  deterministic, in order (same input -> same destination):
  1. path in {archive, spec_revision, canon_mirror}     -> FROZEN (no touch)
  2. dir in {sessions, findings, experiments, evaluation,
     correspondence, historical, incidents}             -> RECORD
  3. extension in {md, pdf, png, tex, bib, html, csv}    -> NARRATIVE/ARTIFACT
  4. extension == py OR executable main()                 -> RUNTIME (home eval)
  5. json/jsonl under state-like path or regenerable      -> RUNTIME/state
  6. basename exists byte-identical (or fused) in system/ -> CONSIDERED -> ARCHIVE
  7. bound by instance.vsm AND logic unique here           -> promote: system/
  8. carries predicates AND logic not yet in system/       -> promote: system/
  9. logic in system/ AND predicates NOT in kernel         -> KERNEL GAP (see sweep S3)
 10. otherwise                                            -> DOCS-LEGIT (stays)

@required_sweeps

  S1 logic-candidates (47): per-doc apply decision tree -> system/ or archive
  S2 binding-repoint map: instance anchors into docs/ — compute which
     moves break bindings-valid; repoint like the s3star circle did
  S3 system -> kernel gap: extract predicates from the 120 system specs,
     compare against vos_kernel runtime checks (today: 3 invariants +
     covenant) -> kernel-work backlog entries (NOT auto-implemented)
  S4 legacy versions (~430): normalize the ones a sweep TOUCHES; the
     rest registered as staged debt (do not churn 430 files blindly)
  S5 runtime homes: 18 .py (keep with their experiment records vs move
     to scripts/) + runtime json/jsonl audit vs .gitignore doctrine
  S6 archive consolidation: after S1/S2, docs/ census re-run ->
     target: only RECORD+NARRATIVE+ARTIFACT+DOCS-LEGIT+FROZEN remain

@execution_as_circles

  circle lifecycle-docs  (S1+S2+S4-touched+S5+S6)  -> docs/ clean
  circle lifecycle-kernel (S3)                      -> kernel gap registered
  both: detect -> fix -> verify -> register, with gates as enforcement:
    bindings-valid (#67), manifest-dest-integrity (#68),
    vsf-knowledge-complete (#69 — content-sha survives moves: a move
    lands in 'relocated', still rc0)

@risks

  - instance bindings break on move (mitigation: S2 repoint BEFORE commit,
    bindings-valid green required)
  - manifest dest stale after moves (mitigation: doc_manifest rescan)
  - write-gates block legacy files touched (mitigation: normalize to
    1.2.1 at transition, same as S5 record normalization)
  - archival = data-loss risk (mitigation: moves only, git history,
    archive dir inside workspace — R17 respected)

@decision_needed_S5

  D-A: archive destination — docs/archive/<cycle>-<ts>/ (chosen here) or
       a second frozen snapshot like spec_revision?
  D-B: normalization scope — only files touched by sweeps (chosen) or
       full 430-file legacy normalization now?
  D-C: experiment .py — stay with records (chosen default) or scripts/?
  D-D: execute both circles now, or lifecycle-docs first and pause?

